repo: https://github.com/open-lm-engine/lm-engine
sha: a9c6e2b81ec33143419f82309706929195a740c0

sha notes:
  a9c6e2b8 is "[MoE] cleanup aux loss (#518)", 2026-09-25. It is also the current
  main HEAD as of 2026-11-18 -- the repo has not moved since that commit -- and it
  is the minimum-diff commit against /app/src of the reference image
  us.icr.io/cil15-shared-registry/lm-engine:0.1.0-cuda-fa2cc (all 494 files that
  the patches below do not touch are byte-identical to it).

patches (applied in order with `git apply`):
  0001 restore lm_engine/training/data/ibm.py from edd51c41^:lm_engine/data/ibm.py
       (IBM/torchtitan scalable dataloader; added in #93 f5d44533, removed in #286
       edd51c41), import paths fixed for the deeper module path.
  0002 get_pretraining_dataloaders routes FSDPDataset/IBMDataset to
       get_ibm_dataloaders.
  0003 MoE expert_frequency cast to int64 before its NCCL all_reduce and the metrics
       add (NCCL rejects UInt32). Was a runtime sed in gbansible
       appwrapper_pretrain.yml.j2.
  0004 non-reentrant activation checkpointing passes determinism_check="none"
       (bf16-forward / fp32-recompute metadata mismatch). Was a runtime sed in
       gbansible.

deviations from the reference image:
  0001 and 0002 reproduce the reference image's two source changes byte for byte.
  0003 and 0004 do NOT exist in the reference image -- both files are byte-identical
  to upstream there, because gbansible sed-patched them at job launch instead. We
  bake them so this recipe does not depend on gbansible. The image built from this
  pin is therefore intentionally not equivalent to :0.1.0-cuda-fa2cc.

not carried:
  the train.py git-metadata guard -- the reference image needed it because its
  Dockerfile used `COPY .` with a .dockerignore that excludes .git. Our
  Dockerfile.gpu clones the repo and checks out the sha above, so /app/src/.git is
  present and the guard is unnecessary (the guard has been offered upstream).
  docker/Dockerfile.bak -- a byte-identical backup of upstream's own Dockerfile that
  the reference image happens to carry. Dead weight.

verify:
  scripts/check-patches.sh clones the repo at the sha above and applies every patch
  in filename order with `git apply`. tests/test_patches.py runs it.
